# The two films: scene list with narration. Visual kinds are drawn by film.html.
LIFE = [
 ("title", "Hello, hello, and welcome, my lovely little organisms, to the Osmotic Expanse. Do settle into your membrane, because this is going to be smashing.", {}),
 ("world", "There is no sun here. No ground. No sky. Just warm, endless soup, as far as the membrane can see. Instead of oceans, the Great Flows: rivers of food that carry you, if you let them. Instead of mountains, protein ranges. Instead of cities, colonies the size of a small planet. Rather swish, isn't it?", {"img": "banner-world", "head": "THE SOUP", "sub": "no sun, no ground, no sky"}),
 ("membrane", "And you, darling, are not a person. You are an organism. Your skin is a membrane, and it decides what gets in and what stays out. Which matters, because out here, everything leaks. The whole game, really, is about staying a bag of water. So keep it zipped.", {"head": "EVERYTHING LEAKS"}),
 ("lineages", "Now, pick your people. The Amoeban: no fixed shape, terribly clever with chemistry. The Epithalian: flat, layered, built like a filing cabinet. The Flagellan: all whips and fins, very fast, very fragile. The Lysosan: quiet, patient, and nobody quite trusts them. The Immunan: spiky, commanding, frightfully literal. And the Barophil: dense, heavy, and absolutely not moving for you.",
   {"cards": [["lineage-amoeban", "AMOEBAN"], ["lineage-epithalian", "EPITHALIAN"], ["lineage-flagellan", "FLAGELLAN"], ["lineage-lysosan", "LYSOSAN"], ["lineage-immunan", "IMMUNAN"], ["lineage-barophil", "BAROPHIL"]], "head": "SIX LINEAGES"}),
 ("coins", "Now, money. Energy is called A T P, and here's the cheeky bit: you pay a toll by letting the gatekeeper digest it. Substrate is the raw stuff: goo, minerals, groceries. And Codon is experience. You never spend it. It simply piles up until, one fine day, you grow.", {"head": "THREE COINS"}),
 ("cards", "The first rule of the Expanse: nothing is wasted. Beat a monster and you harvest it. Harvest enough, and you can graft its parts onto yourself. The beast that nearly ate you on Tuesday becomes the armour that saves you on Wednesday. Treasure, my friends, is evolution you haven't used yet.",
   {"cards": [["m-gnaw-swarm", "GNAW SWARM"], ["m-glaze-medusa", "GLAZE MEDUSA"], ["m-drift-whale", "DRIFT WHALE"], ["m-protease-warden", "PROTEASE WARDEN"]], "head": "NOTHING IS WASTED"}),
 ("pulse", "Of course, the monsters have opinions about all this. Fights are called Pulse Wars: everyone thrashing about in the current, six seconds a round. Get knocked flat and you don't die. You go Dormant, and leak, quite dramatically, until a friend patches you up. Which is why you bring friends.", {"a": "m-cytoplasmic-bleeder", "b": "lineage-flagellan", "head": "PULSE WAR"}),
 ("code", "Civilisation, naturally, has paperwork. The Sacred Code has seven Precepts. Tonicity is truth: you may not lie about what you are. Non-Waste: every body is harvested, or properly buried. The Wardens keep the registers, the Ash collect the dead, and the colonies decide things together, by breathing. More on that in our next little picture.",
   {"img": "order-II", "head": "THE SACRED CODE", "lines": ["1  Containment", "2  Non-Waste", "3  Catalysis is debt", "4  Tonicity is truth", "5  The Code is written", "6  A body is its own argument", "7  The Membrane is mercy"]}),
 ("tide", "And everything changes with the Tide: four seasons of saltiness. In the hypertonic season the whole world dries you out, duels get shorter and meaner, and sensible organisms ration their water. A plan that worked last season might be absolutely suicidal in this one.", {"head": "THE OSMOTIC TIDE"}),
 ("drop", "But here's the real mystery. Long ago, one drop of Prime Serum fell into a mindless puddle, and the puddle learned to keep going. Then, one day, the Serum stopped. Nobody knows why. Whoever finds out could rewrite the whole Expanse. Perhaps, darling, it will be you.", {"head": "WHY DID IT STOP?"}),
 ("end", "This has been the Osmotic Expanse. Stay wet. Stay wonderful. And do mind the membrane.", {}),
]

QUORUM = [
 ("qtitle", "Gather round, my dear organisms, for a little history. This is the story of how the Expanse learned to make up its mind.", {}),
 ("making", "In the beginning, in what the old ones call the Making, there was only warm, mindless chemistry. Over twenty four million Beats it learned a single trick: to keep. The first enclosed volumes. The first membranes. The first organisms. Each one, quite alone.", {"chap": "I", "head": "THE MAKING"}),
 ("gather", "And then, a discovery. A cell alone is a chemistry. A thousand cells that agree are a body. The first colonies were not built, you see. They were agreed.", {"chap": "II", "head": "THE FIRST COLONIES"}),
 ("air", "Here is how they agree. Nobody votes. Not once, not ever. Every organism that cares about a question breathes its signal into the Hearth air. The air thickens. And when it is thick enough with one answer, the whole colony simply knows. All of it, at once, in its chemistry. That, darlings, is a Quorum.", {"chap": "III", "head": "THE HEARTH AIR"}),
 ("track", "The bigger the colony, the more signal it takes. A hamlet tips at four. A metropolis needs ten. A colony that trusts itself agrees sooner. A colony at odds may argue for a very, very long time.", {"chap": "IV", "head": "THE ISSUE TRACK"}),
 ("speaker", "Someone must say it out loud. Enter the Quorum Speaker, who reads the air, and announces. Announces, mind you. Never decides. Every Speaker has an Honesty, from one to six, and everybody discusses it openly, rather like the weather.", {"chap": "V", "head": "THE SPEAKER", "img": "lineage-immunan"}),
 ("unfair", "Now, the scandalous bit. It is not fair. An organism with more energy can breathe more signal. The Swollen breathe as hard as they like. The Dry, if they are clever, buy the air. And all of it, I'm sorry to say, perfectly lawful.", {"chap": "VI", "head": "IT IS NOT FAIR"}),
 ("quench", "Which brings us to the gravest crime in the Expanse. Quenching: breathing an enzyme that destroys the other side's signal before it can build. Not lying in the air, but making the air lie. A found quench voids the Quorum, and the sentence is Unlisting. Ask a certain Corvane how that went.", {"chap": "VII", "head": "BREAKING THE AIR"}),
 ("closing", "Then came the Closing. The Serum stopped, the Sacred Code was issued as law, and the old habit of agreeing hardened into something that binds. Today, to act against a reached Quorum is to act against your own colony's chemistry. You feel it, every time you try.", {"chap": "VIII", "head": "THE CLOSING"}),
 ("convo", "Not everything goes to the air, of course. Smaller matters, a market, a trial, a wedding, are settled in a Convocation: one room, one motion, and three to six parties haggling as if their lives depended on it. Which, frequently, they do.", {"chap": "IX", "head": "CONVOCATION"}),
 ("qend", "So the next time your colony goes quiet, and the Hearth air turns thick and strange, breathe carefully. History is being made. And you, my dear, are in it.", {}),
]

def _s(*pairs): return {"shots": [[f"ui-{i:02d}", fr] for i, fr in pairs]}
UI = [
 ("title", "Right then, my lovely organisms. Let's take a quick tour of your screen at the table. Phone, tablet or laptop: it all works the same way.", {"t1": "HOW TO PLAY", "t2": "AT THE TABLE", "sub": "the player's screen"}),
 ("phone", "When your host shares the link, open it, and type the name the table calls you. Press Join. That's it. No account, no password, no fuss.", {**_s((1, [0, 640, 860, 520]), (2, [0, 640, 860, 520])), "head": "JOIN THE TABLE"}),
 ("phone", "First, session zero. Read it. If anything is too much, say the pause word, Slack Water, and the scene stops, no questions asked. You can also add things to leave out of the game, and nobody is told who asked.", {**_s((3, [0, 120, 860, 620])), "head": "SESSION ZERO"}),
 ("phone", "If you'd rather talk than type, say yes here, and the Talk button will listen through your phone. Then tap: I have read this, and I am ready to play.", {**_s((3, [0, 740, 860, 720])), "head": "READY?"}),
 ("phone", "Now choose your character. In this world it's called an organism. There are four ready-made Hands, each described in plain words: the tough one, the clever one, the fast one and the sharp one.", {**_s((4, [0, 760, 860, 900])), "head": "CHOOSE A CHARACTER"}),
 ("phone", "Tap one, and give it a name, or press Random name until something tickles you. Then press Play this organism.", {**_s((5, [0, 1250, 860, 520])), "head": "NAME YOUR ORGANISM"}),
 ("phone", "This is the Play tab, your home. The Story shows what the Director says, and what everyone does. Underneath is the box where you tell the Director what your organism does, in your own words.", {**_s((6, [0, 170, 860, 560])), "head": "THE STORY"}),
 ("phone", "Type it and press Say, or press Talk and simply speak. No commands. No menus. Just say what you do.", {**_s((7, [0, 380, 860, 300])), "head": "SAY WHAT YOU DO"}),
 ("phone", "When something is uncertain, the Director asks you to roll. This card shows how many dice you get, the number you need to beat, and your chance of success. Press Roll the dice.", {**_s((8, [0, 100, 860, 620])), "head": "YOUR ROLL"}),
 ("phone", "And the app does the arithmetic. Ones count as nothing, and cost you Stress. Anything over the Threshold is Overflow, and it buys you something. Two sixes and no ones? That's Runaway Catalysis. Smashing.", {**_s((9, [0, 960, 860, 520])), "head": "THE RESULT"}),
 ("phone", "Prefer real dice? Tap I rolled my own, roll them on the table, and tap in each die. The app trusts you. Mostly.", {**_s((10, [0, 0, 860, 560])), "head": "YOUR OWN DICE"}),
 ("phone", "Lost? Tap Where you are, for the room, what's in front of you, the distances, and the way out.", {**_s((11, [0, 150, 860, 1250])), "head": "WHERE YOU ARE"}),
 ("phone", "The Sheet tab is your organism: health, energy, Stress, your dice for every skill, your weapon and your kit. It keeps itself up to date, so there's no rubbing out.", {**_s((12, [0, 120, 860, 1050])), "head": "YOUR SHEET"}),
 ("phone", "Story is everything the Cohort has found out so far. Words explains every strange word in plain English, with a search box. And Rolls keeps every throw, in case anybody argues.", {**_s((13, [0, 120, 860, 720]), (14, [0, 120, 860, 1300]), (15, [0, 120, 860, 680])), "head": "STORY · WORDS · ROLLS"}),
 ("phone", "And Colours lets you restyle the whole screen, with a high contrast option, if the soup is hard on the eyes.", {**_s((16, [0, 100, 860, 1100])), "head": "COLOURS"}),
 ("phone", "When a fight starts, a Pulse War appears. On your turn you get Pulse Points, those little circles, and every action shows its price on the button: Strike two, Drift one, Vent one, and so on.", {**_s((17, [0, 620, 860, 1100])), "head": "PULSE WAR"}),
 ("phone", "Tap Strike, pick a target, tap anything that applies to the situation, and Strike. Then roll, exactly as before.", {**_s((18, [0, 880, 860, 760]), (19, [0, 100, 860, 620])), "head": "STRIKE"}),
 ("phone", "A hit! The damage is worked out for you, armour and all. Nobody does sums at this table.", {**_s((20, [80, 580, 700, 640])), "head": "HIT"}),
 ("phone", "When something attacks you, the Incoming card appears. If you held a Reserve on your turn, you can Deflect, Brace or Inhibit. If not, let the dice fall, and be brave about it.", {**_s((21, [0, 100, 860, 620])), "head": "INCOMING"}),
 ("end", "That's the whole screen. Say what you do, roll when you're asked, and leave the sums to us. Now off you go, and do mind the membrane.", {"t1": "SAY WHAT YOU DO.", "t2": "ROLL WHEN ASKED.", "sub": "The Osmotic Expanse"}),
]
